{"name":"10 tuggummi & zamuz - tricked happiness (denkensiefursich mash-up)","date":"2005-11-28T00:25:52.000Z","clearFrame":false,"components":[{"type":"Comment","group":"Misc","text":"Tricked Happiness                                               September 17, 2005\r\n------------------------------                                               --------------------------------\r\n\r\nWhen I saw \"Modern Happiness\" by Zamuz, I instantly thought of Tuggummi's \"Trickery\". So, plain and simply, I combined the two, altered a few lines of code, changed and combined a few effects, and added a bit of my own style.\r\n\r\nWell, this needs a rather high end machine to look good. On the lesser of my two computers I max out at 31.8 fps, but on the other I get near 45. I wonder what I am doing wrong; both presets separetely were fast, but as soon as I touch them and combine them, the speed drops significantly. Oh well, it's all in good fun. If someone wants to sufficiently optimize this, let them and send me the revised version, I would like to see this baby fly!\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n--------------------Original Comments------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n                        Trickery------------------|\r\n                     made for-----------------|\r\n                 singles 2004 ep-----------------|\r\n                    by jukka keskinarkaus--------|\r\n                         22th of July 2004---------|\r\n\r\n\r\n>  visions five\r\n>  modern happiness\r\n>  by zamuz\r\n\r\n>  i was doing a remix for les noobiens some time ago, but it was getting way too far from the original, so i started from scratch and ended up with this. the background is where i got my previous avatar from. feed it some beats."},{"type":"EffectList","enabled":true,"clearFrame":false,"input":"IGNORE","output":"REPLACE","inAdjustBlend":128,"outAdjustBlend":128,"inBuffer":0,"outBuffer":0,"inBufferInvert":false,"outBufferInvert":false,"enableOnBeat":false,"enableOnBe